diff --git a/Docs/OPERATION_SUPPLY_FIXES.md b/Docs/OPERATION_SUPPLY_FIXES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5cb9a64
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Docs/OPERATION_SUPPLY_FIXES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Operation supply and reserve fixes
+
+Against GitLab `1ab4f99a76adb530f86b278390ab8139ef41cc96`. These are source fixes.
+They do not rebuild `CvGameCoreDLL.dll`. Apply after or independently of
+`fixes/0001-source-correctness.patch`; the hunks do not overlap.
+
+## Field armies published no reinforcement demand
+
+`AI_getOperationRoleTarget` skipped any operation whose stack was not standing
+on a plot owned by the same player. A stack on a road between two of your
+cities, on neutral ground, or inside enemy territory therefore created no
+replacement demand. The path query and logistics horizon already reject an
+undeliverable queue. The ownership test was the wrong proxy, and it fired
+exactly when replacements matter.
+
+The replacement is `AIHierarchyPolicy::supplyReachable`: straight-line distance
+against `horizon * baseMoves`, then the existing safe-path and horizon checks.
+A continent-away army does not force an A* from every city.
+
+## A dead commander deleted his own record
+
+`AI_rememberGeneral` returned immediately when `getUnit` failed. Every death
+path calls it and then erases the operation, so the loss never reached the
+agenda. The comment above the career sweep says a death is operational
+evidence. The function now records the career anyway. A later live unit copies
+that record only if it still has the doctrine badge.
+
+## Gold-hurry reserve could overflow
+
+`AI_doGoldHurry` computed `max(0, -calculateGoldRate())` and multiplied by the
+runway. Negating `INT_MIN` is undefined, and a large late-game deficit times
+the speed multiplier overflows signed 32-bit before the comparison with
+`AI_goldTarget`. `AIDecisionPolicy::deficitReserve` saturates.
+
+## Not changed on purpose
+
+Commissioning and resurrecting great generals with `initUnit`, without spending
+great-person points, is explicit in `AI_updateMilitaryOperations`. It is a
+balance defect, not an accidental inverted condition. Removing it is a design
+change and is not in this patch. `AI_doCentralizedProduction` still returns
+immediately; the body below it is unfinished, not a dormant switch.
